the bush here in northern kenya has  become  almost a desert the iwasu-niyero river  reduced to little more than a trickle  for years now the area  has had far too little rain  shepherd abdiabkula keeps his goats  close to the water  at least there's something for the  animals to graze on here  and he never strays far from his village  these days we fear for our safety  our neighbors the samburu community keep  attacking us  they kill and steal our livestock  to help de-escalate the conflicts habiba  tadicha  often reaches out to the shepherds along  the river she used to head the local  nature conservancy  and is well known in the region disputes  over water and grazing land  have become frequent here she negotiates  with shepherds in this area of bellico  bulesa  while other women are in dialogue with  nearby communities  we have many meetings these meetings  especially like bilikobules i'm leading  like sarah there is a lady called  pauline who is leading  so even though because we are mother  and we know the disadvantages and  advantages of the  conflict so we decide to sit with our  young ones those who are leading in  conflict  our husbands and that's what makes this  unusual  women are taking the lead and making a  difference  the kenyan constitution upholds gender  equality  but in practice it's still the exception  the kenyan branch of the environmental  group tnc  is led by munira angonge she says kenya  needs more women leaders like habiba  tadicha  they're actually raising their voices  making decisions  on how their conservancies can be  managed especially for example if  there's a conservancy that  has tourism facilities and they get  conservation fees  there's the issue of sharing of those  proceeds between the operations of the  conservancy  and a percentage goes back to the  communities so that they can you know  invest in education health facilities  and others the tnc  runs 39 major conservancies in kenya it  also finances the one  in habiba toda's the conservancies  protect nature  offer job prospects and encourage women  to play a greater role in society  habiba tadicha benefited from the  conservancy and is now helping others  she and other women in her village have  built a culture center  [Music]  they did a lot of the work themselves  the women rent out the hall and the  lodges to visitors and local people  which brings in money  that's allowed them to set up a savings  club here the women give out loans to  each other  using income from the culture center  subsidies from ngos  as well as members own savings  leads the club she's given loans of 250  dollars to more than a hundred women  mostly to finance small business  ventures  dani roba got a loan from the savings  club to invest  in an electric motor for her corn mill  now she can earn more money  like so many here she's benefited from  the nature conservancy  melania in the beginning the local  community here was opposed to the  establishment of a conservancy  but habiba lobbied for it so that women  could benefit  she's very brave one time she was even  shot at  but she wasn't intimidated and just  carried on with her work  we're very happy now  tadicha doesn't want to talk about the  threats she's received  she'd rather focus on being a role model  for the next generation  at the local school she encourages  children not to give up  even when they face opposition  girls don't allow yourselves to be left  behind  and don't be shy all the time during her  time as head of the local nature  conservancy  habiba tadica secured funding for two  more classrooms here  today she's part of the council of  elders and has arranged financial help  for children from poorer families  to attend school those who have  prospects for the future she says  are less likely to engage in conflict  education is the best thing in our life  in everybody's life because  illiteracy  illiteracy to make stuff even not to  uplift our standards  for one  getting education you have you  you get jobs earning some salaries  uplifting your standard and even  additional of education  to everything is important if not  education  i myself i cannot be a leader of my  community  she loves her work but is often rushed  off her feet  she has three children and also cares  for her sick husband  then she has two small shops that she  opened with loans  from the savings club thankfully her  eldest daughter is able to help out  habiba tadicha hopes her daughter will  follow in her footsteps  and she certainly seems to have  inherited her mother's passion for  leadership  she already leads the local youth group  you
 

